   "": {
    "actClause": "AN ACT to amend the tax law, in relation to imposing an additional real estate transfer tax within the county of Essex",
    "basePrintNo": "S5869",
    "basePrintNoStr": "S5869-2009",
    "coSponsors": {
     "items": [],
     "size": 0
    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "Add Art 31-B-1 §§1448-g - 1448-u, Tax L",
    "lawSection": "Tax Law",
    "memo": " BILL NUMBER:  S5869\n\n TITLE OF BILL :\nAn act to amend the tax law, in relation to imposing an additional\nreal estate transfer tax within the county of Essex\n\n\n PURPOSE :\nTo authorize the Essex County Board of Supervisors to adopt a local\nlaw providing for the imposition of a real estate transfer tax.\n\n SUMMARY OF PROVISIONS :\nSection one - adds a new article 31-B-1 of the tax law to read as\nfollows: Tax on Real Estate Transfers in the County of Essex\n\nSection two - contains the effective date\n\n JUSTIFICATION :\nThe Essex County Board of Supervisors has requested introduction of\nthis legislation to allow the county to adopt a local law to impose,\ncollect and retain a tax on real estate transfers of $1.00 for each\n$500.00 of consideration on real property transactions in Essex County\nwith the proceeds of the said tax to be used for the new Essex County\nPublic Safety Radio Communications system.\n\n LEGISLATIVE HISTORY :\nNew bill.\n\n FISCAL IMPLICATIONS :\nNone to the State.\n\n LOCAL FISCAL IMPLICATIONS :\nThe county estimates this will generate approximately $641,000 in\nrevenue.\n\n EFFECTIVE DATE :\nThis act shall take effect immediately.\n",
